stage: 7
finding: The last human can leave a bot-only room ticking with its links and Worlds still live until server stop: room-host.ts includes bots in count(), then uses that count as the leave/expiry retirement guard. In a two-room loopback variation at the cheap budget, expiring the leader's hold correctly handed off to the remaining human and preserved the bot; after that human left, the old room still contained the bot, had no leader, and both rooms' bot links closed only on stop. The stage check passes because it removes the bot before the last human leaves. Define and cover retirement when the last active or held human is gone; capacity accounting should continue to count bots.
